title: Lessons adopted from 'How the Claude Code team does code review' (claude.dev, 2026-10-15)
summary: |-
  The founder shared Anthropic's Claude Code code-review post. It is captured in neurons as s:web-9a73944324 and digested into 10 neurons under r:ai/agents/code-review: n:review-as-risk-routing, n:human-time-guardrail-metric, n:verify-before-review, n:verified-review-findings, n:review-must-converge, n:risk-tier-set-by-change, n:incidents-as-reviewer-eval, n:review-md-and-fix-at-source, n:explainers-replace-diff-reading, n:approval-circuit-breaker.

  It validates existing Gnomon/Paradigm choices:
  - verify before claiming done (probes, file ground truth);
  - verified findings (re-check reviewer claims);
  - agent approval never counts as human, and approval is bound to content (contentHash);
  - always-human sensitive paths (gate-class);
  - noise scored by author response (Loid override calibration);
  - incidents as eval (the Warpline outcome taxonomy);
  - the merge queue gap (Warpline's semantic adjudication).

  Adopted and scheduled:
  - T-2026-10-17-003: per-PR fresh-context review in our build, with a 3-round cap and Aegis required on security PRs.
  - T-004: spec v3.9 armada convergence rule, an evidence-driven gate-tightening circuit breaker, and test/risk/revert fields on briefs and cards.
  - T-005: REVIEW.md generated from .purpose and aspects.
  - T-006: auto-propose a fix-at-source on repeated findings.
  - T-007: a staged npm `next` channel.

  Also scheduled: T-008, the D83 kernel-log implementation (ordering-not-flush, boot-session classification, G-LOG-11) after the human-cadence probe.
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
  - '#kernel-log'
learnings:
  - Agent-author plus agent-reviewer loops need a hard round cap and diff-only re-review, or they churn on old code (Claude Code saw 50+ overnight rounds, 59% of repeat findings were pre-existing).
  - Approval should be bound to the exact content, and an agent's approval must never fill a human slot; Gnomon's contentHash-bound, human-only approve already encodes this.
